WEBVTT

00:00.790 --> 00:02.330
Al, here.

00:07.500 --> 00:09.150
What's up with that dagger?

00:09.550 --> 00:11.390
Isn't the hook on the wrong side?

00:11.390 --> 00:14.270
You're right. It is an unusual design.

00:14.270 --> 00:16.220
It's a right-handed stiletto.

00:16.220 --> 00:18.520
Since the halberd is strong, but unwieldy.

00:18.520 --> 00:21.650
And... who did this dagger belong to?

00:21.940 --> 00:23.400
My father.

00:24.910 --> 00:26.380
I can't accept this!

00:26.690 --> 00:29.150
It's a memento, isn't it?

00:29.150 --> 00:30.990
Yeah, but...

00:31.920 --> 00:36.270
I feel like it's better off 
in your hands, somehow.

00:39.580 --> 00:40.750
It's okay.

00:41.270 --> 00:45.060
I've already received plenty 
of valuable things from him.

00:53.320 --> 00:58.870
The Faraway Paladin

00:55.160 --> 00:58.870
<b><u>The Lord of the Rust Mountains</u></b>

02:16.150 --> 02:23.240
Asleep Beneath the Water

02:18.620 --> 02:22.900
Anyway, let's finish up before 
the others come back with food.

02:26.490 --> 02:29.590
You could have just let 
me take care of all this.

02:29.900 --> 02:32.040
It'll go faster if we work together.

02:32.480 --> 02:35.130
Besides, you're royalty, aren't you?

02:35.130 --> 02:36.910
Only in name.

02:36.910 --> 02:40.530
I've often wondered why I couldn't 
have been born to a family

02:40.530 --> 02:42.690
that ran a simple workshop.

02:42.690 --> 02:47.340
And if you'd been born to a family that 
ran a simple workshop, you'd think,

02:47.340 --> 02:51.150
"Maybe I'm actually a prince descended 
from the royalty of some fallen nation,

02:51.150 --> 02:54.240
and it is my duty to rebuild my kingdom!"

02:56.390 --> 03:01.240
I'd want to tell myself that 
it's not as great as it sounds.

03:01.790 --> 03:04.870
But you'll still do it, right?

03:04.870 --> 03:06.720
Yes, I will.

03:06.720 --> 03:09.660
In truth, all of my people 
long for their homeland.

03:10.060 --> 03:14.760
If putting my life on the line 
will set their souls alight,

03:14.760 --> 03:18.000
I think that would be truly wonderful.

03:19.120 --> 03:23.040
But I feel as if I've dragged 
you into my own problems.

03:23.040 --> 03:24.380
You haven't.

03:24.380 --> 03:27.280
I knew I'd have to fight, too.

03:28.040 --> 03:29.960
If I abandoned all this now,

03:29.960 --> 03:33.270
I'd never be able to face 
my parents or Gus again.

03:33.670 --> 03:36.010
Besides, I want to take pride in myself.

03:36.010 --> 03:38.780
When I return to the goddess 
of light's side one day,

03:39.080 --> 03:42.110
I want to proudly tell her I 
lived my life the best I could.

03:42.110 --> 03:43.980
Show off a little, you know?

03:44.810 --> 03:47.480
So I won't run from the 
dragon. I'll fight it.

03:48.510 --> 03:50.840
It's thanks to you that I was 
able to make that decision.

03:51.210 --> 03:52.300
Thank you.

03:53.560 --> 03:56.050
I should be the one to thank you.

03:56.550 --> 03:58.660
I swear on your father's dagger

03:58.660 --> 04:01.770
that no matter how this ends, 
I will regret nothing.

04:01.770 --> 04:04.190
Good. I trust you to have my back.

04:04.190 --> 04:05.310
I'll be counting on you.

04:09.030 --> 04:09.920
Right!

04:11.200 --> 04:12.410
You guys!

04:17.110 --> 04:18.420
I'm back.

04:28.450 --> 04:30.770
Hey, don't feel bad that 
you didn't catch any fish.

04:30.770 --> 04:31.810
It was a fluke.

04:31.810 --> 04:32.780
Indeed.

04:35.900 --> 04:39.280
Well, great warriors aren't 
always great fisher—

04:39.280 --> 04:41.010
I <i>said</i> it was a fluke. Got it?

04:41.010 --> 04:42.090
Uh, right.

04:43.900 --> 04:47.170
But... how did you fell this deer?

04:47.170 --> 04:48.900
Huh? Oh...

04:48.900 --> 04:51.880
I concealed my presence and 
kinda just walked into it.

04:51.880 --> 04:54.880
Then I fired by pure reflex,

04:54.880 --> 04:57.680
and it was as if its heart just 
pulled the arrow right toward it.

04:57.680 --> 05:00.110
You certainly have the blessings 
of the god of spirits...

05:00.110 --> 05:02.200
He just got lucky.

05:02.200 --> 05:04.730
And luck was not on our side.

05:06.550 --> 05:10.140
Just admit you suck at 
fishing. You'll feel better.

05:10.140 --> 05:11.300
It was <i>a fluke</i>.

05:11.860 --> 05:13.870
You just don't know when to give up.

05:16.130 --> 05:19.290
Now, now, leave them be.

05:19.290 --> 05:21.030
That's so like you, Reystov.

05:30.310 --> 05:33.110
Are you afraid of me, Will?

05:33.110 --> 05:35.180
No, not at all.

05:35.510 --> 05:37.480
Yes, of course not.

05:39.600 --> 05:40.800
Listen to me.

05:41.470 --> 05:47.180
Humans have flesh that feels warm 
to the touch, and they breathe.

05:47.470 --> 05:49.970
Get used to the appearance of humans.

05:49.970 --> 05:55.310
The friends you'll make one day 
won't look like the three of us.

05:57.090 --> 06:00.210
It's okay. I'm not afraid of you, Mary.

06:00.610 --> 06:03.430
I won't be afraid of any 
people I meet, either.

06:05.510 --> 06:08.300
That puts my mind at ease.

06:09.800 --> 06:14.560
Will, you might feel regretful one day.

06:14.560 --> 06:15.450
Huh?

06:15.450 --> 06:20.730
Valor is the strength to destroy 
injustice, but it's also a curse.

06:21.460 --> 06:22.730
A curse?

06:23.180 --> 06:26.660
There are times when you can't give 
up because you know you're strong,

06:26.660 --> 06:28.800
even if means your own death.

06:29.910 --> 06:33.530
I'm only teaching you how to 
fight because it's what I want,

06:33.530 --> 06:35.920
so if it ever comes to that, 
feel free to hate me.

06:36.610 --> 06:40.870
Blood, there's no way I could ever hate you!

06:41.530 --> 06:42.610
That so?

06:56.660 --> 06:58.090
I'm home.

06:59.450 --> 07:02.290
Mary, I actually made some friends.

07:03.670 --> 07:06.760
Blood, it's thanks to you 
that I've made it this far.

07:07.620 --> 07:11.240
It's tough not having you two 
around, but I'm managing.

07:12.190 --> 07:15.350
Because I remember the last 
things you both said to me.

07:15.760 --> 07:18.710
I'll keep seeing them through... so...

07:21.670 --> 07:23.020
I'm going now.

07:24.930 --> 07:26.910
Gus, you were here?

07:27.530 --> 07:29.120
You're leaving, then?

07:29.600 --> 07:30.760
In the morning.

07:30.760 --> 07:34.350
Valacirca is a warmonger 
through and through.

07:34.350 --> 07:37.210
He can only survive amidst the chaos of war.

07:37.660 --> 07:40.580
It's unlikely you can avoid a fight...

07:40.580 --> 07:46.310
and the only one who might even 
pose a threat to him is you.

07:46.310 --> 07:49.400
But as I am now, I'm not strong enough.

07:49.400 --> 07:54.270
I'd be an easy obstacle for a dragon 
to overcome, even if he was hesitant.

07:54.580 --> 07:59.340
You will die. Both you and your friends.

07:59.340 --> 08:03.520
And even if you survive, 
someone else might die.

08:04.750 --> 08:07.280
This place is your last stop.

08:08.110 --> 08:09.730
You could run away.

08:12.300 --> 08:16.450
If I threw away everything to survive, 
it would just mean I wasn't dead.

08:16.810 --> 08:20.690
And I learned in both my past life and 
this one that that's not good enough.

08:22.020 --> 08:25.020
I'm pretty sure all the 
others feel the same way.

08:25.590 --> 08:30.360
Al, Menel, Reystov, and Ghelreis... 
They've all come prepared.

08:30.800 --> 08:32.680
Maybe even more so than me.

08:33.430 --> 08:37.430
Besides, none of us have 
any intention of dying.

08:37.950 --> 08:41.510
Honestly... Who did you take after, boy?

08:42.430 --> 08:43.620
Good question.

08:43.620 --> 08:49.430
In that case, your only chance is now, 
before his wound has fully healed.

08:49.430 --> 08:52.700
The eye wound that King Aurvangr gave him...

08:53.210 --> 08:54.370
Yes.

08:55.030 --> 09:00.170
How deeply I wish that I could 
go with you and help you out...

09:00.170 --> 09:03.860
But I am of no use to you 
when it matters the most.

09:05.220 --> 09:07.820
Just hearing you say that is enough.

09:08.390 --> 09:13.010
It's okay. You can just wait 
here with Blood and Mary.

09:13.010 --> 09:14.000
Yes.

09:14.870 --> 09:16.550
I'll be waiting.

09:28.480 --> 09:29.400
Let's go.

09:53.110 --> 09:55.610
We need to take this tributary, right?

09:55.610 --> 09:57.160
Going by the map, yes.

09:57.630 --> 10:00.160
If we see any changes in the 
terrain, we'll turn back.

10:00.760 --> 10:01.560
Right.

10:02.380 --> 10:04.750
Sylphs, sylphs, put the wind at our backs,

10:04.750 --> 10:07.110
to accompany us as we make our way.

10:13.300 --> 10:16.950
Do you have a guess as to 
what we might find up ahead?

10:19.050 --> 10:22.080
I know nothing beyond the Great Collapse.

10:22.670 --> 10:24.150
Okay.

10:24.150 --> 10:26.790
However, before the Great Collapse,

10:26.790 --> 10:30.370
there was an elven forest to 
the west of the Iron Country.

10:30.370 --> 10:32.310
It was called Lothdor.

10:32.310 --> 10:35.490
Lothdor? As in, "land of flowers"?

10:35.490 --> 10:37.840
You know the elven language?

10:37.840 --> 10:40.740
Enough to get by. Gus taught me.

10:40.740 --> 10:44.250
Lothdor? I've heard of it.

10:44.250 --> 10:49.140
"Pass through the Iron Country, 
where dwarfs live in caves,

10:49.140 --> 10:53.840
cross the shining rainbow 
bridge, and there is Lothdor.

10:54.370 --> 10:59.140
Lyres of silver and flutes of gold 
sing the song of Remmirath."

11:00.030 --> 11:01.260
What's that?

11:01.260 --> 11:03.450
A travel song known throughout my homeland.

11:03.450 --> 11:06.140
Ah, that song brings back memories.

11:06.140 --> 11:08.800
Though the Iron Country did not have

11:08.800 --> 11:11.130
a very good relationship 
with the elves of Lothdor.

11:11.130 --> 11:13.690
Oh, because of all the logging?

11:13.690 --> 11:15.460
You know the history well.

11:15.460 --> 11:19.520
Nah. Something similar 
happened in my own homeland.

11:19.850 --> 11:23.190
Skirmishes between our peoples 
grew violent at times.

11:23.190 --> 11:25.360
Sometimes there was only hatred between us.

11:25.360 --> 11:28.810
But at the same time, they 
were still our neighbors.

11:29.510 --> 11:33.130
They excelled at song and the spirit arts,

11:33.130 --> 11:35.780
yet they were a proud, ill-tempered people.

11:36.240 --> 11:39.750
We had a certain respect for them,

11:39.750 --> 11:42.970
and they surely felt the same way about us.

11:43.680 --> 11:45.680
And during the Great Collapse?

11:46.280 --> 11:50.120
I only know they secluded themselves 
in the forest and resisted.

11:50.120 --> 11:53.100
They absolutely would not give up.

11:53.870 --> 11:58.690
Perhaps they survived. 
Elves live long lives.

11:58.690 --> 11:59.950
Maybe even—

12:12.860 --> 12:15.170
Is no one there?

12:15.570 --> 12:17.660
I don't... see anyone...

12:22.670 --> 12:24.320
How regrettable.

12:25.140 --> 12:29.290
It looks like the river's 
flow changed in 200 years.

12:33.420 --> 12:36.260
You know, this scenery looks familiar.

12:37.090 --> 12:38.380
Words of Taboo?

12:38.380 --> 12:39.230
Yeah.

12:39.230 --> 12:42.640
If the elves really secluded themselves 
in the forest, no one could do anything.

12:42.640 --> 12:48.740
So those damned immoral demons used the 
Words of Taboo to rot the entire forest.

12:48.970 --> 12:50.210
We have to destroy them.

12:50.210 --> 12:52.890
You said it. We can't let them live.

12:52.890 --> 12:54.950
But first...

12:54.950 --> 12:55.830
Yeah.

13:08.230 --> 13:08.920
There!

13:10.930 --> 13:12.030
A serpent?!

13:12.030 --> 13:13.950
Don't gawk! There are more coming!

13:20.860 --> 13:22.020
Menel! Full speed!

13:22.020 --> 13:22.760
I know!

13:23.160 --> 13:25.250
Sylphs, sylphs, put the wind at our backs,

13:25.250 --> 13:27.270
to accompany us as we make our way!

13:28.270 --> 13:30.080
Damn it! The response is too slow!

13:30.080 --> 13:31.580
Focus on the incantation!

13:31.580 --> 13:33.780
Reystov and Ghelreis, take the port side!

13:33.780 --> 13:35.360
Al, back up Menel!

13:36.580 --> 13:38.530
<i>We're in a real pinch here.</i>

13:38.530 --> 13:39.800
<i>It's risky, but...</i>

13:40.260 --> 13:40.920
Vastar—

13:40.290 --> 13:40.920
<b>Devasta—</b>

13:45.550 --> 13:46.000
Will!

13:51.380 --> 13:54.180
<i>I can't see a thing... In which case...</i>

14:14.150 --> 14:15.220
Sir Will!

14:19.270 --> 14:20.300
You all right?

14:28.920 --> 14:30.050
Vastare.

14:29.050 --> 14:30.050
<b>Devastate</b>

14:36.940 --> 14:37.870
There.

14:37.870 --> 14:39.700
You're merciless, man.

14:39.700 --> 14:41.280
I have to be.

14:41.280 --> 14:43.990
Menel, let's move carefully.

14:43.990 --> 14:44.690
Yeah.

14:46.820 --> 14:50.900
Um, the water suddenly 
turned clear back there...

14:50.900 --> 14:53.330
Huh? That was just a prayer of cleansing.

14:53.330 --> 14:54.330
Huh?!

14:54.330 --> 14:57.650
Isn't a prayer of cleansing only 
strong enough for a bottle's worth,

14:57.650 --> 14:59.410
or at most, a small pond?

14:59.410 --> 15:00.480
Uh...

15:00.480 --> 15:02.330
He brute-forces things. Get used to it.

15:02.570 --> 15:03.920
Right...

15:03.920 --> 15:05.520
He looks so calm,

15:05.520 --> 15:08.910
but he uses some straight-up 
barbarian tactics to brute-force things.

15:08.910 --> 15:10.060
I'm used to it by now.

15:10.060 --> 15:11.300
That's just mean.

15:11.300 --> 15:13.770
The river has swallowed up the forest.

15:14.260 --> 15:16.630
The change in the terrain here is a problem.

15:16.630 --> 15:20.160
Ghelreis, do you see anything 
that looks familiar?

15:20.580 --> 15:21.660
No...

15:22.140 --> 15:24.100
Not in this mess.

15:26.980 --> 15:28.360
What about that?

15:33.920 --> 15:38.690
That style of architecture... 
It's definitely elven.

15:38.690 --> 15:40.520
Where are we on the map?

15:41.210 --> 15:44.200
I would say... right about here.

15:45.480 --> 15:49.060
Which means... that's the way we need to go.

15:50.080 --> 15:54.120
The fae around here are weakened. 
I can't call on them.

15:54.120 --> 15:57.330
Maybe if I could use my 
Lord of the Forest powers...

15:57.330 --> 16:01.500
No, we probably shouldn't try 
to clean this up any more.

16:01.500 --> 16:04.240
We might catch the demons' attention.

16:04.660 --> 16:05.520
Well, then...

16:07.350 --> 16:08.720
Let's row.

16:32.240 --> 16:33.250
Enemies?

16:34.180 --> 16:37.720
No. They're just in pain.

16:42.520 --> 16:45.520
It's all right. Everything's all right now.

16:45.520 --> 16:48.520
None of you will curse anyone anymore.

16:48.520 --> 16:50.860
You won't haunt. You won't torment.

17:01.350 --> 17:03.640
I'll take care of things from here.

17:03.640 --> 17:05.580
You can just rest now.

17:07.580 --> 17:11.630
Gracefeel, goddess of light, 
grant them peace and guidance.

17:52.100 --> 17:55.590
We should go that way, then? 
As quickly as possible?

18:08.350 --> 18:11.350
Please grant us the blessing of your light.

18:24.980 --> 18:28.500
Let's go! Full speed in that 
direction! Now! Move it!

18:28.500 --> 18:29.240
Huh?

18:29.240 --> 18:31.500
Don't trust an elf's sense of time!

18:31.500 --> 18:33.340
Sylphs, sylphs, put the wind at our backs!

18:33.340 --> 18:35.450
Accompany us with all haste and speed!

18:37.410 --> 18:39.220
You know the saying, 
"When an elf says, 'Wait a sec,'

18:39.220 --> 18:40.940
he really means 'See you in a year'"?

18:40.940 --> 18:42.940
That's a true story!

18:43.140 --> 18:45.700
So when someone with such 
a lousy sense of time

18:45.700 --> 18:48.050
says "as quickly as possible," you—

18:50.180 --> 18:52.130
I knew it, damn it!

18:52.510 --> 18:55.950
Maidens of water, give us your blessing! 
Race with us over the surface!

19:00.020 --> 19:01.780
Row! Hurry!

19:16.520 --> 19:17.660
Menel!

19:18.300 --> 19:19.290
Is he oka—

19:19.290 --> 19:20.190
It's not dead!

19:28.290 --> 19:29.060
Damn it!

19:34.820 --> 19:36.140
It's coming! Brace yourself!

19:41.040 --> 19:41.790
A hydra?

19:41.790 --> 19:43.440
Sagitta Flammeum!

19:42.030 --> 19:43.160
<b>Flame Arrow</b>

19:47.780 --> 19:49.180
Fire is effective!

19:49.180 --> 19:52.170
Al, Ghelreis, Reystov! Stay in front!

19:52.170 --> 19:54.520
Menel, take him and swap with me!

19:54.520 --> 19:55.160
Got it!

19:55.160 --> 19:58.490
I'll stay in the rear and burn the heads!

19:58.490 --> 20:00.060
The rest of you, stay in front!

20:00.060 --> 20:00.740
Got it!

20:01.210 --> 20:01.950
Right!

20:02.680 --> 20:03.800
I'm on it!

20:11.730 --> 20:13.230
<b>Flame Arrow</b>

20:11.750 --> 20:13.230
Sagitta Flammeum!

20:16.730 --> 20:18.240
Now, young master!

20:22.760 --> 20:23.890
Wow...

20:23.890 --> 20:27.220
Well, looks like I'm not 
needed here anymore.

20:27.220 --> 20:29.150
But that's fine. 
I don't wanna waste my arrows.

20:38.920 --> 20:40.030
Did we kill it?

20:40.030 --> 20:41.400
Do not let your guard down.

20:41.400 --> 20:45.430
A hydra's poison cannot be neutralized 
by your everyday miracle.

20:45.720 --> 20:50.430
A snake like this can still fight 
even when all its heads are cut off.

20:51.000 --> 20:54.960
You don't wanna get hurt 
fighting its death throes.

20:57.070 --> 20:57.950
Will!

20:58.810 --> 21:01.310
Take her! She's been bitten!

21:02.960 --> 21:05.290
Hang in there! I'll heal you right away!

21:08.090 --> 21:09.830
You... can't...

21:10.460 --> 21:13.840
Hydra poison... deadly...

21:14.150 --> 21:18.340
<i>This is bad. The prayer of healing 
won't work if she refuses it.</i>

21:18.340 --> 21:19.880
Stop talking!

21:21.500 --> 21:22.780
No...

21:23.280 --> 21:28.350
North... my people's... village...

21:28.350 --> 21:32.180
Seriously, stop! 
Just let him help you, brethren!

21:33.230 --> 21:35.860
Breth...ren?

21:36.550 --> 21:38.640
He's no ordinary priest.

21:38.640 --> 21:42.770
Fellow forest dweller, you can be saved. 
So accept his miracle.

21:44.570 --> 21:45.660
Pray!

23:35.680 --> 23:39.970
The Land of Flowers
